WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.900
In the year 383, Fu Jian led the great Former Qin army — said to number a million — marching south to attack Jin in mighty force.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:17.370
Unexpectedly, at the Fei River, the Qin army was badly defeated by the Jin army, and its soldiers scattered and fled in every direction.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.280
Fu Jian fled in panic with his remnant troops, trembling with fear all along the way.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:35.230
Looking back, the grasses and trees on Mount Bagong, in his eyes, had all turned into Jin soldiers coming after him.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.510
Terrified, he hurriedly urged everyone to run faster, and they fled even more quickly.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:49.340
Later generations used the idiom 'every bush and tree looks like an enemy soldier' to describe how, in extreme panic, a person suspects danger everywhere.

